-- push rax; pop rcx with the code at any address below 2^44 and the stack anywhere in [3·2^45, 3·2^45 + 2^44)
-- (every address and every word given by its bits): rcx is rax, by refl. The two zones keep a code
-- address and a stack address apart in a bit no offset reaches, and every address canonical.
sym-state : Word → Word → Word → X86
sym-state a ip sp = x86-set-rax a (x86-set-rsp sp (x86-set-rip ip (x86-poke #2 ip #22864 x86-user64)))
